# A flat deck with TWO round boundaries across it (M16 Step 1).
#
# A fixture, not content: `playtest_bridge.seg` says in its own header that tests
# keep their own segments so tuning that one for feel can never break the gate.
#
# TWO STRIPS AND NOT ONE, because every question the round machine asks is about
# the NEXT boundary -- `gate_after` is the whole API -- and a segment with one
# strip cannot tell a correct implementation from one that always returns the
# only answer it has. Same reason the plinko feature shipped with balls ghosting
# through each other: every test used a single ball.
#
# They are 8 rows apart so "the next one" is unambiguous, and neither sits at row
# 0 or at the last row, where an off-by-one in either direction would still land
# on something.

name = test_gate
base_height = 0
width = 10
length = 14
tags = foot, test, gate

